// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-055
// title: BACnet/IP Gateway
// date: 2026-04-03
// status: accepted

#context
Building-automation devices (HVAC, AHU, VAV, chillers) speak BACnet/IP over UDP 47808.
Existing gateways (Modbus, OPC-UA, MQTT) follow model→manager→NATS sensor.raw pattern (ADR-043).
BACnet can be added with the same pattern using the node-bacnet package.

#decision
Add BACnet/IP gateway following the established gateway pattern:
- Model: IBacnetGateway — host, port, objects (objectType/instanceNumber/property/field), polling
- Manager: BacnetGatewayManagerService — dynamic import of node-bacnet, poll presentValue
- Routes: /bacnet-gateways CRUD + /start /stop /test /status /read
- NATS publish: sensor.raw.${deviceId} with source='bacnet'
- Auto-device-registration (same as Modbus) when applicationId set

#consequences
~New package: node-bacnet added to apps/api/package.json
~BACnet objects map objectType+instanceNumber+property → field name in sensor.raw
~readProperty callback wrapped in Promise (node-bacnet is callback-based)
~If node-bacnet not installed: dynamic import throws friendly error at startGateway
~Front-end: BacnetGatewayTable/Modal/DetailPanel + useBacnetGateways hook
~Sidebar: 'bacnet' entity item added to application sub-nav
~No impact on existing gateways or Processing Engine
